{
  "description": "serializer binding-record SHAPE vectors — they exercise the record schema + the one cross-field semantic, NOT a real binding (there is no records/ yet; a real record lands later and its authority begins only then). Coordinates are synthetic but well-formed. One positive (a valid forward binding) and eleven negative controls, each pinned to the exact rejection token the validator emits, so every rule is proven able to fail: required fields, complete source_ref coordinates (a bare digest is rejected — every reference must carry repository+revision+path+sha256), hex patterns, the qualification.vectors == serializer_contract.vectors pre-image identity, the rejection of a free-form-string qualification, the non_retroactivity and method consts, owner-neutral rejection of extra fields, a non-zero vector count, and rejection of the pre-review bare-digest field shape.",
